# The scenes of the contract-tests-between-teams deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# contract-tests-between-teams.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in contract-tests-between-teams.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: step 1, the version catalogue
note "Step 1: add Pact JVM to the version catalogue."
show libs.versions.toml "/pact/" gradle/libs.versions.toml

## Scene 2: step 2, the test dependencies
note "Step 2: Pact's JUnit libraries, one for the *consumer*, one for the *provider*."
show lessons/contract-tests-between-teams/example/build.gradle.kts "/^dependencies/" "lesson build file" --zoom 10-11

## Scene 3: the consumer's code
note "The code under test, the consumer: the order screen reads *available* from the stock service."
show StockClient.java 26 33 "the order screen's client" --zoom 32

## Scene 4: the provider's code today
note "The provider: today's stock service. A tidy-up *renamed* the field."
show TodaysStockBodies 9 14 "today's stock service" --zoom 13

## Scene 5: the order screen's weak tests
note "The order screen's *weak* tests, against a stand-in its own team wrote."
show HandWrittenStockService 14 16 "the order screen's stand-in" --zoom 16
show StockClientTest 19 22 "the order screen's weak tests"

## Scene 6: the stock service's weak tests
note "The stock service's own *weak* tests: the status code and the item's code."
show StockServiceTest 36 49 "the stock service's weak tests" --zoom 41-43

## Scene 7: the consumer's pact test
note "The *strong* tests, the consumer's side: each answer the order screen relies on, in a pact."
show StockClientPactTest 21 35 "the order screen's pact" --zoom 31-34
show StockClientPactTest 37 42 "the order screen's pact test"

## Scene 8: the published pact
note "The pact file, published as a *versioned artifact*. A folder stands in for the package repository."
show lessons/contract-tests-between-teams/example/package-repository/order-screen-pacts/1.0.0/order-screen-stock-service.json 20 42 "the pact, version 1.0.0" --zoom 22,35-40
show lessons/contract-tests-between-teams/example/build.gradle.kts 35 40 "the step that stands in for publishing" --mark 35-39

## Scene 9: the provider's pact test
note "The *strong* tests, the provider's side: every interaction replayed against the real service."
show StockServicePactTest 18 44 "the stock service's pact test" --zoom 19

## Scene 10: the pact check names the field
note "Run every test against today's stock service:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:contract-tests-between-teams:test -Pcode=today"
callout "Each team's own tests pass. The pact check names the field the order screen reads and the service no longer sends."

## Scene 11: the fixed stock service
note "The stock service that keeps the field the pact names:"
show AgreedStockBodies 9 15 "the fixed stock service" --zoom 13
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:contract-tests-between-teams:test"
callout "The service meets the pact again. Drop the old field only when no supported order screen reads it."
